    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d492">

                <pb facs="0671" n="601" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg601"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Pike.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 48.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-04-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 2, 1862</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of March 12 (No. 41) has been
                    received. Your account of the system of finance and revenue existing in the
                    Netherlands is very interesting. In the belief that it may prove useful in the
                    present emergency, I shall take pleasure in procuring its submission to
                    Congress.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">James S. Pike</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c, &amp;c, &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
